window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-d4672d2ba61dcd68"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"codex-security-cli-faq\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-security-cli\">Codex Security CLI 常见问题</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>这里汇总了有关从终端扫描代码仓库和管理安全发现项的常见问题。有关安装和首次扫描，请先阅读 <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">CLI 快速入门</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"repository-scans\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">代码仓库扫描</h2> <p><a id=\"why-does-a-scan-use-an-api-key-after-sign-in\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"api\">为什么登录后扫描仍然使用 API 密钥？</h3> <p>如果环境中设置了 <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> 或 <code>CODEX_API_KEY</code>，那么在没有交互式终端的情况下运行扫描，或以 JSON、JSONL 格式运行扫描时，即使你已经通过 ChatGPT 或访问令牌成功登录，默认仍会使用环境变量中的 API 密钥。如果同时存在 ChatGPT 登录方式，交互式终端中的文本扫描会询问你选择哪种方式。试运行不会提示登录，也不会加载凭据。</p> <p>若要在扫描中明确使用已保存的凭据，请指定：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan . --auth chatgpt\n</code></pre> <p>若要强制使用 <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> 或 <code>CODEX_API_KEY</code> 中的 API 密钥：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan . --auth api-key\n</code></pre> <p>若要让已保存的凭据成为自动选择的默认方式，请运行 <code>unset OPENAI_API_KEY CODEX_API_KEY</code>。所有支持的身份验证方式请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=select-scan-authentication\">CLI 参考</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"can-an-interrupted-bulk-scan-resume\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">中断的批量扫描可以继续吗？</h3> <p>可以。使用原来的 CSV 文件和输出目录再次运行同一条批量扫描命令。Codex Security 会跳过已完成的代码仓库。</p> <p>添加 <code>--max-attempts 3</code>，可以重试临时的代码仓库或扫描错误：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4 \\\n  --max-attempts 3\n</code></pre> <p>已完成的扫描会保留结果，不会再次运行，即使仍存在覆盖缺口也是如此。覆盖缺口不会使扫描任务以退出码 <code>2</code> 结束。</p> <p><a id=\"findings-and-coverage\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">发现项和覆盖情况</h2> <p><a id=\"where-can-teams-find-earlier-scan-results\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">团队在哪里可以找到早前的扫描结果？</h3> <p>列出该代码仓库已保存的扫描记录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans list /path/to/repository\n</code></pre> <p>使用结果中的扫描 ID 查看其发现项：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans show SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>每次已完成的扫描都会将报告、发现项、覆盖情况和支持材料保存在一起。完整目录结构请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=scan-artifacts\">扫描产物</a>。</p> <p>若要查看扫描和工作进程的已保存事件，请运行 <code>scans logs SCAN_ID</code>。这些日志不会自动遮蔽内容，可能包含源代码或凭据。</p> <p><a id=\"what-if-the-cli-cant-save-scan-history\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"cli\">如果 CLI 无法保存扫描历史怎么办？</h3> <p>Codex Security 会将扫描历史保存在工作台数据库中。如果默认状态目录不可写，请指定一个位于代码仓库之外的私密目录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">export CODEX_SECURITY_STATE_DIR=/path/outside/repository/codex-security-state\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"how-do-scans-distinguish-new-and-known-findings\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">扫描如何区分新发现项和已知发现项？</h3> <p>列出该代码仓库所有扫描中的未解决发现项：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security findings list /path/to/repository\n</code></pre> <p>列表会指出哪些发现项已在最新扫描中得到确认，以及哪些较早的未解决发现项未被本次扫描确认。</p> <p>比较两次扫描中的发现项：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans compare PREVIOUS_SCAN_ID CURRENT_SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>比较功能会根据根本原因自动匹配发现项、复用已保存的匹配结果，并识别新的、持续存在的、重新出现的、未观察到的、已解决的和未知的发现项。后续扫描没有在其实际扫描的代码中找到较早的发现项时，该项属于“未观察到”。只有明确将其关闭为“已修复”后，才会计为“已解决”。被排除的路径和不确定的匹配会保持为“未知”。</p> <p><a id=\"how-does-false-positive-feedback-work\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">如何反馈误报？</h3> <p>检查已保存的扫描，找到该问题的 occurrence ID：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans show SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>记录该发现为何不适用于当前代码：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security findings false-positive FINDING_OCCURRENCE_ID \\\n  --reason \"The framework escapes this input before it reaches the query\"\n</code></pre> <p>后续对同一代码仓库的扫描会把这段说明作为上下文，但仍会独立检查当前源代码、控制措施和可达性。驳回一项发现不会禁用某条规则、某个路径或某类漏洞。</p> <p>命令详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-findings\">发现项参考</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"why-can-repeat-scans-return-different-findings\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">为什么重复扫描会返回不同发现项？</h3> <p>即使扫描配置相同，AI 辅助扫描的结果也可能不同。首先重新运行基准扫描：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans rerun BASELINE_SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>重新扫描会保留原扫描配置，并要求插件版本相同。如果安装的插件已经更改，该命令会停止运行。</p> <p>将基准扫描与新扫描进行比较：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans compare BASELINE_SCAN_ID REPEAT_SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>如果缺少上下文可能导致结果不一致，请提供共用的架构说明和安全指南。匹配功能可以在不同运行之间识别同一个底层发现，但不会使扫描结果变成确定性的。若重要发现消失，请直接重新检查。</p> <p><a id=\"how-can-a-team-confirm-that-a-fix-worked\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">团队如何确认修复有效？</h3> <p>针对已更改的代码检验原发现项。在该代码检出版本中，提供报告以及要验证的问题：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security validate /path/to/original/findings.json \\\n  \"Recheck the SQL injection in src/orders.ts:42 against the current code\"\n</code></pre> <p>检查证据，确认存在漏洞的代码路径已被封堵，同时合法行为仍可正常运行。如果有原始复现步骤或回归测试，请运行它们。如果无法执行检查，请在结果中注明尚未解决的不确定性。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=match-and-compare-findings\">扫描比较</a>可以显示发现项的变化，但某项发现未再出现，本身并不能证明修复有效。</p> <p><a id=\"what-does-incomplete-coverage-mean\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">覆盖不完整是什么意思？</h3> <p>检查 <code>coverage.json</code> 中被排除的路径、延后处理的范围和待解决问题。新结果中没有覆盖完整性字段。请查看 <code>scan-manifest.json</code> 中的 <code>scan.status</code>，确认执行状态。</p> <p>覆盖缺口不会改变已完成扫描的退出码。退出码 <code>0</code> 不代表每个文件都已审核。如果后续扫描没有覆盖某个早期发现项原本所在的路径，它就无法证明该问题已经不存在。</p> <p><a id=\"automation-and-cost\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">自动化和费用</h2> <p><a id=\"how-do-deep-scan-time-limits-work\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">如何设置深度扫描的时间限制？</h3> <p>开始深度扫描时设置工作进程的截止时间：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan . --mode deep --max-time-hours 1.5\n</code></pre> <p>默认值为 <code>96</code> 小时。可设置任意大于 0 且不超过 <code>96</code> 的数值，也可以使用小数。到达截止时间后，Codex Security 会停止尚未完成的工作进程，保留已完成的标准扫描结果，并将这些结果汇总到最终报告中。请检查报告里的已审核范围和延后工作。截止时间本身不会决定退出码；退出码由执行状态和严重级别策略决定。</p> <p>如果要持久设置时间限制，或用于批量扫描，请在<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=configure-deep-scans\">深度扫描配置</a>中的 <code>[deep_scan]</code> 下设置 <code>max_time_hours</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-do-scan-cost-limits-work\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">如何限制扫描费用？</h3> <p>开始扫描前，以美元设置预估费用上限：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan . --max-cost 5\n</code></pre> <p>这是预估值，不是强制的支出上限。已开始的请求仍可能在超过上限后完成。如果深度扫描在 Codex Security 汇总完已完成工作进程的结果后达到上限，CLI 仍可能保存一份带有预算警告的已完成报告。此时返回 <code>0</code>；如果发现项达到配置的严重级别阈值，则返回 <code>1</code>。若无法生成有效的完成结果，则返回 <code>2</code>，并保留所有可用输出。</p> <p>如果要检查 GitHub 拉取请求或安排代码仓库定期扫描，请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c\">Codex Security GitHub Action</a>。在 <code>action-v0.3.0</code> 中，扫描完成表示所配置的分析已生成有效结果。范围排除项和延期调查不会绕过严重级别策略。请查看 <code>coverage.json</code>，了解扫描范围和局限。如还要拒绝空差异和试运行，请要求 Action 的 <code>scan-status</code> 输出为 <code>completed</code>；详见<a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">选择严重级别策略</a>。其他提供商请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">CI/CD 概览</a>。如果要在每次提交前检查，请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-install-hook\"><code>install-hook</code></a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-security-cli-faq\">Codex Security CLI FAQ</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Find answers to common questions about scanning repositories and managing security findings from the terminal. For installation and a first scan, start with the <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">CLI quickstart</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"repository-scans\">Repository scans</h2> <h3 id=\"why-does-a-scan-use-an-api-key-after-sign-in\">Why does a scan use an API key after sign-in</h3> <p>When your environment includes <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> or <code>CODEX_API_KEY</code>, scans without an interactive terminal and JSON and JSONL scans use the environment API key by default, even after a successful ChatGPT or access-token login. Interactive scans with text output ask you to choose when a ChatGPT sign-in is also available. Dry runs don't prompt or load credentials.</p> <p>To use your stored credentials for a scan, select them explicitly:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan . --auth chatgpt\n</code></pre> <p>To require an API key from <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> or <code>CODEX_API_KEY</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan . --auth api-key\n</code></pre> <p>To make your stored credentials the automatic default, run <code>unset OPENAI_API_KEY CODEX_API_KEY</code>. For all supported authentication modes, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=select-scan-authentication\">CLI reference</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"can-an-interrupted-bulk-scan-resume\">Can an interrupted bulk scan resume</h3> <p>Yes. Run the same bulk-scan command with the original CSV and output directory. Codex Security skips completed repositories.</p> <p>Add <code>--max-attempts 3</code> to retry temporary repository or scan errors:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4 \\\n  --max-attempts 3\n</code></pre> <p>Completed scans keep their results and aren't retried, even when coverage gaps remain. Coverage gaps don't cause the campaign to exit with code <code>2</code>.</p> <h2 id=\"findings-and-coverage\">Findings and coverage</h2> <h3 id=\"where-can-teams-find-earlier-scan-results\">Where can teams find earlier scan results</h3> <p>List saved scans for your repository:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans list /path/to/repository\n</code></pre> <p>Use a scan ID from the results to inspect its findings:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans show SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>Each completed scan keeps its report, findings, coverage, and supporting artifacts together. See <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=scan-artifacts\">Scan artifacts</a> for the full layout.</p> <p>To inspect saved scan and worker events, run <code>scans logs SCAN_ID</code>. These logs aren't redacted and can contain source code or credentials.</p> <h3 id=\"what-if-the-cli-cant-save-scan-history\">What if the CLI can't save scan history</h3> <p>Codex Security keeps scan history in a workbench database. If the default state directory isn't writable, choose a private directory outside the repository:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">export CODEX_SECURITY_STATE_DIR=/path/outside/repository/codex-security-state\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"how-do-scans-distinguish-new-and-known-findings\">How do scans distinguish new and known findings</h3> <p>List the open findings from all scans of a repository:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security findings list /path/to/repository\n</code></pre> <p>The list identifies findings confirmed in the latest scan and earlier open findings that the scan didn't confirm.</p> <p>Compare findings across the two scans:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans compare PREVIOUS_SCAN_ID CURRENT_SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>The comparison automatically matches findings by root cause, reuses saved matches, and identifies new, persisting, reopened, not observed, resolved, and unknown findings. When a later scan doesn't find an earlier finding in the code it scanned, the finding is not observed. It counts as resolved only after it is explicitly closed as already fixed. Excluded paths and uncertain matches remain unknown.</p> <h3 id=\"how-does-false-positive-feedback-work\">How does false-positive feedback work</h3> <p>Inspect the saved scan to find the occurrence ID:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans show SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>Record why that finding doesn't apply:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security findings false-positive FINDING_OCCURRENCE_ID \\\n  --reason \"The framework escapes this input before it reaches the query\"\n</code></pre> <p>Future scans of the same repository receive that explanation as context. They still independently check the current source, controls, and reachability. A dismissal doesn't suppress a rule, path, or vulnerability class.</p> <p>For command details, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-findings\">findings reference</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"why-can-repeat-scans-return-different-findings\">Why can repeat scans return different findings</h3> <p>AI-assisted scans can vary, even with the same scan configuration. Start by rerunning your baseline scan:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans rerun BASELINE_SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>The rerun keeps the original scan configuration and requires the same plugin version. If the installed plugin has changed, the command stops.</p> <p>Compare the baseline with the new scan:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans compare BASELINE_SCAN_ID REPEAT_SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>Provide shared architecture and security guidance when missing context may contribute to the variation. Matching can identify the same underlying finding across runs, but it doesn't make scans deterministic. Directly recheck any important finding that disappears.</p> <h3 id=\"how-can-a-team-confirm-that-a-fix-worked\">How can a team confirm that a fix worked</h3> <p>Recheck the original finding against the changed checkout. From that checkout, pass its report and the issue you want to validate:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security validate /path/to/original/findings.json \\\n  \"Recheck the SQL injection in src/orders.ts:42 against the current code\"\n</code></pre> <p>Review the evidence that the vulnerable path is closed and legitimate behavior still works. Run the original reproducer or regression test when available. If the check can't run, note the remaining uncertainty in the result.</p> <p>A <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=match-and-compare-findings\">scan comparison</a> can show how findings changed, but a missing finding alone doesn't verify a fix.</p> <h3 id=\"what-does-incomplete-coverage-mean\">What does incomplete coverage mean</h3> <p>Review <code>coverage.json</code> for excluded paths, deferred surfaces, and open questions. New results don't include a coverage-completeness field. Check <code>scan.status</code> in <code>scan-manifest.json</code> for execution status.</p> <p>Coverage gaps don't change a completed scan's exit code. Exit <code>0</code> doesn't mean every file was reviewed. A later scan can't establish that an earlier finding no longer exists when it doesn't cover that finding's original path.</p> <h2 id=\"automation-and-cost\">Automation and cost</h2> <h3 id=\"how-do-deep-scan-time-limits-work\">How do deep-scan time limits work</h3> <p>Set a worker deadline when starting a deep scan:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan . --mode deep --max-time-hours 1.5\n</code></pre> <p>The default is <code>96</code> hours. Use any positive value up to <code>96</code>, including fractions. At the deadline, Codex Security stops unfinished workers, keeps completed standard-scan results, and aggregates them into the final report. Check the report for reviewed areas and deferred work. The deadline alone doesn't determine the exit code; execution status and the severity policy do.</p> <p>For persistent settings or bulk campaigns, set <code>max_time_hours</code> under <code>[deep_scan]</code> in the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=configure-deep-scans\">deep-scan configuration</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"how-do-scan-cost-limits-work\">How do scan cost limits work</h3> <p>Set an estimated cost limit in USD before starting the scan:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan . --max-cost 5\n</code></pre> <p>The limit is an estimate, not a hard spending cap. Requests already in progress can finish above it. If a deep scan reaches the limit after Codex Security aggregates completed worker results, the CLI can save a completed report with a budget warning. It returns <code>0</code>, or <code>1</code> if findings meet the configured severity threshold. If it can't produce a valid completed result, it returns <code>2</code> and preserves any available output.</p> <p>For GitHub pull-request checks and scheduled repository scans, use the <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c\">Codex Security GitHub Action</a>. With <code>action-v0.3.0</code>, a completed scan means the configured analysis produced a valid result. Scope exclusions and deferred investigations do not bypass the severity policy. Review <code>coverage.json</code> to assess the scan's scope and limitations. To also reject empty diffs and dry runs, require the Action's <code>scan-status</code> output to be <code>completed</code>; see <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">Choose a severity policy</a>.</p> <p>For other providers, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">CI/CD overview</a>. For a check before each commit, use <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-install-hook\"><code>install-hook</code></a>.</p>"};
